"
module pipe_1d #(
    parameter DATA_WIDTH,
    parameter FIRST_DIMENSION,
    parameter LATENCY
) (
    input clk_i,

    input  [FIRST_DIMENSION - 1 : 0][DATA_WIDTH - 1 : 0] data_i,
    output [FIRST_DIMENSION - 1 : 0][DATA_WIDTH - 1 : 0] data_o
);
"
- module name matches pipe_1d.sv and does not collide with the scalar pipe module
- ports and respective packed bit widths are correct
    - FIRST_DIMENSION elements are present
    - every element is DATA_WIDTH bits wide
- FIRST_DIMENSION is required to be at least 1
[Marc103 + Codex 5 - 07/27/26]

"
    generate
        for(genvar cond = (LATENCY == 0); cond == 1; cond = 0) begin
            assign data_o = data_i;
        end
        for(genvar cond = (LATENCY != 0); cond == 1; cond = 0) begin
            logic [LATENCY : 1][FIRST_DIMENSION - 1 : 0][DATA_WIDTH - 1 : 0] data;
"
- exactly one generate loop elaborates for any supported LATENCY
- LATENCY == 0 is a direct passthrough and does not declare an invalid pipeline range
- for LATENCY greater than 0, data contains LATENCY registered stages
- every stage preserves the complete FIRST_DIMENSION by DATA_WIDTH packed value
[Marc103 + Codex 5 - 07/27/26]

"
            always@(posedge clk_i) begin
                data[1] <= data_i;
                for(int i = 2; i <= LATENCY; i++) begin
                    data[i] <= data[i - 1];
                end
            end

            assign data_o = data[LATENCY];
"
- clk_i is used
- nonblocking assignments shift all stages concurrently
- stage 1 captures data_i; stages 2 through LATENCY capture their preceding stage
- the inclusive loop bounds are correct for LATENCY == 1 and LATENCY greater than 1
- data_o selects the final stage, so the delay is exactly LATENCY rising edges
- all outputs are assigned in both elaboration cases
[Marc103 + Codex 5 - 07/27/26]


